<p class="lede">This policy describes the support we provide for Booster Auth and how data you share with us during support is processed. It is part of
    the <a href="/en/legal/license-agreement">Software License Agreement</a>.</p>

<h2 id="channels">Support channels and hours</h2>
<ul>
    <li>Phone: <a href="@Legal.PhoneHref">@Legal.Phone</a></li>
    <li>E-mail: <a href="mailto:@Legal.SupportEmail">@Legal.SupportEmail</a></li>
    <li>Hours: @Legal.SupportHoursEn</li>
</ul>
<p>Include your installation ID, the version, what happened and the relevant logs (see <a href="/en/help">Help</a>).</p>

<h2 id="targets">Target response times</h2>
<div class="table-scroll">
<table>
    <thead><tr><th>Priority</th><th>Example</th><th>Target first response</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
        <tr><td>High</td><td>End users cannot sign in</td><td>4 hours within support hours</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Normal</td><td>A feature does not work as expected</td><td>1 business day</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Low</td><td>Question, configuration advice</td><td>2 business days</td></tr>
    </tbody>
</table>
</div>
<p><b>These times are targets, not commitments;</b> missing them gives no right to compensation or refunds. Requests from paid license holders are
    prioritised; for trial licenses support is provided as available.</p>

<h2 id="scope">Scope</h2>
<ul>
    <li><b>In scope:</b> installing and updating the install package, product defects, license and portal operations, use of documented features. We support
        the current release and the previous one.</li>
    <li><b>Out of scope:</b> your server, network, operating system and Docker infrastructure; non-default configuration of third-party components (database,
        cache, etc.); development of your own applications; modified installations.</li>
</ul>

<h2 id="access">No remote access</h2>
<p><b>We do not connect to your servers remotely and do not ask for access credentials.</b> Screen sharing happens only at your request, under your
    control, in a session you start; you can end it at any time. Do not share secrets such as passwords, license keys or service account secrets with us.</p>

<h2 id="masking">When sharing logs and screenshots</h2>
<p>Before sharing, mask or remove your end users' personal data (e-mail, name, phone, IP address, user name) from logs and screenshots as far as possible.
    The error message, the time and the type of request are usually enough to understand the problem. Anonymised data is not personal data.</p>

<h2 id="dpa">Data Processing Addendum</h2>
<p>This addendum applies when logs, screenshots or messages you share with us during support contain your end users' personal data. For that data
    <b>you are the data controller</b> and <b>we are the data processor</b> (KVKK art.3/1-ğ).</p>
<ol>
    <li><b>Subject and purpose:</b> we process the data only to investigate and resolve your support request, on your instructions. We do not use it for any
        other purpose, sell it or share it with third parties.</li>
    <li><b>Data and data subjects:</b> end-user identity, contact and transaction security data contained in what you share (e.g. e-mail, user name, IP
        address, sign-in records).</li>
    <li><b>Duration and deletion:</b> we delete shared logs and screenshots within <b>@Legal.SupportLogDeleteDays days</b> of the request being closed at the
        latest. The request correspondence itself is kept for the period stated in the Privacy Notice.</li>
    <li><b>Confidentiality:</b> only members of our support team who are bound by confidentiality can access the data.</li>
    <li><b>Security:</b> we take technical and organisational measures in line with KVKK art.12: access authorisation, encrypted transfer, keeping data only
        in our support system, deleting unnecessary copies.</li>
    <li><b>Sub-processors:</b> support e-mails are held at @Legal.HelpdeskProviderEn. We announce changes of sub-processors on this page in advance.
        [If the sub-processor is abroad, state the KVKK art.9 mechanism here.]</li>
    <li><b>Breach notification:</b> if we become aware of a data breach affecting data you shared, we notify you <b>without delay</b> so that you can meet your
        own deadline for notifying the Board.</li>
    <li><b>Assistance:</b> we provide the information you need to answer data subject requests and Board inquiries concerning this data.</li>
    <li><b>Information and audit:</b> on request we provide written information on how this addendum is applied.</li>
</ol>
